   150	## 4. The 4+34 effective-root coefficients
   151	
   152	The Tschirnhausen-normalized T2 is
   153	
   154	```text
   155	T2=G^3-F^2+(a1*F+a0)*G+(b1*F+b0),
   156	```
   157	
   158	where the displayed `c0*G^2` coefficient has been set to zero.  The four
   159	adjoined chart variables are `T2_a1,T2_a0,T2_b1,T2_b0`.  In normalized form,
   160	
   161	```text
   162	U2=s^396*T2
   163	  =KG^3-KF^2
   164	   +T2_a1*s^66*KF*KG
   165	   +T2_a0*s^264*KG
   166	   +T2_b1*s^198*KF
   167	   +T2_b0*s^396.
   168	```
   169	
   170	The last column begins after the target window, but `T2_b0` remains adjoined
   171	as required by the global effective-root shape.
   172	
   173	For T3 write
   174	
   175	```text
   176	T3=G^9-F^6+sum_{i=2}^9 sum_m T3_a{i}_m{m} F^m G^(9-i),
   177	0<=m<=floor(2i/3), excluding (i,m)=(9,6).
   178	```
   179	
   180	Here `alpha_1=0`, and `(9,6)` is excluded because the coefficient of `F^6`
   181	is already the fixed monic `-1`.  The index rule gives exactly **34** free
   182	coefficients.  In `U3=s^1188*T3`, a column `(i,m)` receives shift
   183	`s^(132*i-198*m)`.
   184	
   185	The expensive monic faces are cancelled algebraically before expansion:
   186	
   187	```text
   188	KG^3-KF^2 = 3*H^4*EG+3*H^2*EG^2+EG^3-2*H^3*EF-EF^2,
   189	KG^9-KF^6 = (KG^3-KF^2)*(KG^6+KG^3*KF^2+KF^4).
   190	```
   191	
   192	This is where the requested subleading jets enter; the face spans alone do
   193	not supply `p^5` or `p^10*q1`.  The shapes and coefficient counts are the
   194	printed approximate-root data audited against Moh p.152 and Xu section 7.3.
