   196	## 5. Coefficient-wise polynomial bridge ideal
   197	
   198	The emitted equations are literal coefficients in the chart ring:
   199	
   200	```text
   201	E2=U2-s^391*p^5                         modulo s^392,
   202	E3=U3-s^1178*p^10*q1                    modulo s^1179  (J0=1 form),
   203	```
   204	
   205	or, before normalizing the nonzero would-be Jacobian constant term,
   206	
   207	```text
   208	E3=U3-s^1178*kappa*p^10*q1,
   209	J0-kappa=0,  Zck*c*kappa-1=0.
   210	```
   211	
   212	For every occurring pair `(n,k)`, the row is `[s^n*pi^k]E2` or
   213	`[s^n*pi^k]E3`.  Consequently all lower coefficients vanish and every
   214	coefficient of the target polynomial is matched, including target powers
   215	that do not otherwise occur.  There is no pi quotient and no pi-degree cap.
   216	The only bookkeeping quotient is `s^392=0` for T2 or `s^1179=0` for T3;
   217	because all normalized inputs have nonnegative `s` support, normal form after
   218	every product determines all coefficients through the respective target
   219	exactly.
   220	
   221	The full rows are polynomial and generally nonlinear in the 869 chart
