   108	used here: at ramification denominator `e=2`, the Galois action sends
   109	`pi -> -pi` and must preserve the root multiset with multiplicities.  A
   110	`[2,1]` multiset cannot be stable because both the double and simple fixed
   111	root would have to be `0`.  Thus the `delta=5/2` split is forced to
   112	`[1,1,1]` with
   113	
   114	```text
   115	p(pi)=pi(pi^2-c),  c != 0.
   116	```
   117	
   118	The gauge `pi -> lambda*pi` sets `c=1`.  I kept a variable `split_c` in the
   119	Singular localizer and imposed `split_c-1`; saturation used
   120	`T*gamma*split_c-1`, so both the split scale and Jacobian scalar are localized.
